### limit.concurrency

Get or set the concurrency limit.

### limit.onIdle()

Returns a promise that resolves when the queue is empty and all running functions have completed.

An active or reserved slot counts as busy, so the returned promise only resolves once both `activeCount` and `pendingCount` are `0`. Calling this when the limiter is already idle returns a promise that resolves immediately.

This is useful when you want to wait for all currently scheduled work to settle, for example before shutting down.

```js
import pLimit from 'p-limit';

const limit = pLimit(1);

limit(() => doSomething());
limit(() => doSomethingElse());

await limit.onIdle();
// All tasks have completed
```

